@startuml Sequence Diagram - GraphRAG Query Flow
!theme vibrant
title Sequence Diagram - GraphRAG

actor "Engineer" as User
participant "Frontend\n(React)" as Frontend
participant "GraphRAGController" as Controller
participant "GraphRAGService" as GraphRAG
participant "EmbeddingService" as Embedding
participant "GraphTraverser" as Traverser
participant "JenaService" as Jena
participant "ContextBuilder" as Context
participant "ClaudeService" as Claude
participant "Claude API\n(Anthropic)" as ClaudeAPI
database "Knowledge Graph\n(Apache Jena TDB2)" as KG

User -> Frontend: Ask question\n"What equipment is affected\nif Substation_123 fails?"

Frontend -> Controller: POST /api/graphrag/ask\n{question: "..."}
activate Controller

Controller -> GraphRAG: processQuery(question)
activate GraphRAG

== Step 1: Generate Query Embedding ==
GraphRAG -> Embedding: generateEmbedding(question)
activate Embedding
Embedding --> GraphRAG: queryEmbedding[]
deactivate Embedding

== Step 2: Find Relevant Entities ==
GraphRAG -> Jena: executeSparqlSelect(\n"SELECT ?s WHERE {...}")
activate Jena
Jena -> KG: Query entities\nmatching "Substation_123"
KG --> Jena: Entity URIs
Jena --> GraphRAG: List<Entity>
deactivate Jena

== Step 3: Retrieve Subgraph Context ==
GraphRAG -> Traverser: traverse(\nstartNode="Substation_123",\ndepth=3)
activate Traverser

loop For each hop (max 3)
  Traverser -> Jena: executeSparqlConstruct(\n"CONSTRUCT {...}")
  activate Jena
  Jena -> KG: Get connected triples
  KG --> Jena: RDF triples
  Jena --> Traverser: Subgraph model
  deactivate Jena
end

Traverser --> GraphRAG: relevantSubgraph
deactivate Traverser

== Step 4: Build LLM Context ==
GraphRAG -> Context: buildContext(subgraph)
activate Context

Context -> Context: formatForLLM(triples)
note right
  Formats RDF triples into
  readable text for Claude:

  "Substation_123 (110kV):
   - Connected to: Line_456
   - Powers: 3 transformers
   - Serves: 2500 consumers
   - Critical equipment: Yes"
end note

Context --> GraphRAG: formattedContext
deactivate Context

== Step 5: Query Claude AI ==
GraphRAG -> Claude: queryWithContext(\nquestion, context)
activate Claude

Claude -> Claude: buildPromptWithContext()
note right
  Prompt structure:

  System: "You are a power grid expert..."

  Context: "[Graph data here]"

  Question: "What equipment affected..."
end note

Claude -> ClaudeAPI: POST /v1/messages\n{model, messages, context}
activate ClaudeAPI

ClaudeAPI -> ClaudeAPI: Process with Claude 3.5 Sonnet
note right
  Claude analyzes:
  - Graph relationships
  - Dependencies
  - Critical equipment
  - Impact severity
end note

ClaudeAPI --> Claude: LLM Response
deactivate ClaudeAPI

Claude --> GraphRAG: Enhanced Answer
deactivate Claude

== Step 6: Build Response ==
GraphRAG -> GraphRAG: buildGraphRAGResponse(\nanswer, context, sources)

GraphRAG --> Controller: GraphRAGResponse {\n answer,\n context,\n sources,\n confidence\n}
deactivate GraphRAG

Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 200 OK\n{JSON response}
deactivate Controller

Frontend -> Frontend: Display answer\n+ visualization
Frontend --> User: Show result with\ngraph visualization

== Alternative Flow: Error Handling ==
alt SPARQL Query Fails
  Jena --> GraphRAG: SparqlExecutionException
  GraphRAG --> Controller: Error response
  Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 500
  Frontend --> User: "Error executing query"
else Claude API Fails
  ClaudeAPI --> Claude: API Error (429, 500)
  Claude --> GraphRAG: ClaudeApiException
  GraphRAG --> Controller: Fallback response\n(without LLM)
  Controller --> Frontend: HTTP 200 (partial)
  Frontend --> User: "Graph data only\n(LLM unavailable)"
end

note over User, KG
  **Total Flow Time: ~2-5 seconds**
  - Embedding: 100ms
  - Graph retrieval: 500-1000ms
  - Context building: 200ms
  - Claude API: 1-3s
  - Response formatting: 100ms
end note

@enduml
